o, are expected to produce numerous showers and\nembedded thunderstorms. Heavy rain falling on saturated soils and\nburn scars could lead to localized flash flooding and rises on\nlocal rivers.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-30T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4e0b211dcd7bab58026a9cb01526038e869174d9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4e0b211dcd7bab58026a9cb01526038e869174d9.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-27T23:59:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 272359 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 559 PM MDT Sun Sep 27 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Warmer and drier conditions continue today. - Increased moisture will arrive by Monday, bringing widespread moderate to heavy precipitation through midweek. - Chances of prolonged rainfall increases flooding concerns in southeast Utah and southwest Colorad","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-27T19:37:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... A few isolated showers and thunderstorms are possible this afternoon, mostly over the high terrain. This evening showers are expected over the central and northern Divide. A strong push of moisture will allow for widespread precipitation Monday and Tuesday. Prolonged rainfall is possible, which increases concerns of flooding, particularly in southeast Utah and southwest Colorado. Th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"hot02","station_name":"CSU Rogers Mesa Research Sta","distan